            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0568" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/806: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-14T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                                1922—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:53 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>95. Your January 13, 4 p.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d187-f1"/> In an interview with
                    the President this morning he expressed his gratification at the proposed action
                    and stated that the invitation when extended would be accepted with pleasure
                    without qualification.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
